; Game text set in a <samp> element keeps its bytes, as quoted game text does
; (TYPO-2). The bad line is prose writing a dash in ASCII; the good line is the
; game's own title text, hyphens included, set as a text diff in <samp>.
;
; Bad:  12  an ASCII dash in prose
; Good: 17  the same hyphen inside <samp>, which is reported by nothing
[Page:Release]
PageContent=#INCLUDE(ReleaseContent)

[ReleaseContent]
<div class="paragraph">
The title screen names the author - and then the artist.
</div>

#TABLE(default,centre)
{ =h Text | =h Change }
{ The title text | <div class="text-diff"><samp class="text-del">SAMPLE GAME - WRITTEN BY A. CODER</samp><samp class="text-ins">SAMPLE GAME 2 - EXTRA LIVES EDITION</samp></div> }
TABLE#
